IAM 
1. Shared access with same account: create  new user account with one root account , so we don't have shared root account credentials. 
2. Granular permission for access : granting different level access to different users as per role in the organisation.
3. Secure access to AWS application : to give secure access to AWS application . for eg : give access to EC2 instance but not to S3 bucket then he can access only EC2 instance.
4. Multifactor authentication( MFA ) : MFA to provide extra level of security for your account. for eg : OTP for bank money transfer, even we have account users and password but OTP require to complete money transfer
5. Identity Federation : using existing account to create new account : for eg : login in some account via google account or via facebook. 
6. Identity information for assurance : for log records 
7. PCI- DSS complance : For online payment rule regulations : for eg some save card. 
8. Eventualy consistent : highly available : 
9: Free to use : IAM is free to use.  													   
													   
