** What is Multiple ZA in RDS 

>> You can select multiple AZ only during RDS DB instance launch . 
>> RDS create standby in different AZ and configure synchronous replication between primary and standby DB instance. standy DB is five minutes behind primary. 
>> You can't read /write standby/seconday  RDS DS instance storage . 
>> You can't select standby RDS  availablity zone, but secondary RDS will be visible after it's creation.
>> Depending upon the instance class , it may take one to few minutes for failover to standby instance. 
>> AWS recommend to use provisional iops storage in multiple AZ. 
   
  Note : When standby instance take over , it will treated as primary storage and it's standby will be created in different AZ, however if failed primary storage came online within time then it will act as standby now. 


** When multiple AZ triggers 
1. In case of failure of primary DB instance failure 
2. In case of AZ failure 
3. Loss of network connectivity to primary DB . 
4. Loss of primary EC2 instance failure. 
5. EBS failure of primary DB instance. 
6. Primary DB setting changed. 
7. Patching of OS of DB instance . 
8. Manual failover ( incase of rebooting ) 

** setting to do to get seamless service during primary DB failover. 
>> It is recommended to use of CNAME to refer your DB instance rather than it's IP address. 
>> Because CNAME doesn't change  , because RDS endpoint doesn't change.   

Note : Primary and standby have different IP address ,but have same CNAME or url address. 



** RDS DB failover alerts 
>> When RDS DB failover , it will send notification  via SNS ( simple notification service ) , it is chargeable service . 
>> In API or CLI you can check logs of RDS DB for last 14 days whereas via AWS console logs for only one day is available. 
>> In case on OS patching , system upgrades or DB scaling horizontally , then this happens at standby first, then at primary . 
>> In multiple AZ , snapshot and automated backup are done at standby instance to I/O suspension on primary . 


** Multiple AZ RDS deployment and maintenance 
>> Firstly maintenance are performed at standby . 
>> After maintenance of standby completed , it will became primary and other DB maintenance will take place. 
>> Manually maintenance of DB RDS via AWS console 
   RDS--> DBS instance--> Modify DB --> set DB Engine version 
>> Software upgradation  are preformed at seconday and primary DB at the same time. It is done during maintenance window , when no . users accessing app is low and to avoid outage. 
   Note : Maintenance window is not inculded in SLA. 
   
   
** RDS backup  methods
>> Automated Backup 
>> Manual backup 
>> Either you can take backup of entire DB instance or for DB. 
>> You can create a storage volume snapshot of your entire DB instance . 
   Note : Automated backup are stored at multiple AZ for data durability . 
>> select --> automated backup at AWS consle. 
>> automated backup are stored at S3. 
>> Multiple AZ automated backup are taken from standby DB 
>> DB instance must be in ACTIVE state at the time of automated backup. 
  Note : In single DB , automated backup taken from it, it DB is not reachable during the time. 
>> automated Backup time can be select by user. 
>> No addtional cost for RDS automated backup. 
>> Automated backup deleted at the time of DB instance deletion . 
>> Outage occured if the automated retention period changes from zero to non zero value. 
>> Retention period is 7 days by default. aws aurora -- 1 day via console 
>> Retention period range 0-35 days 


** Manul snapshot in RDS 
>> In case of manual snapshot ,point in time recovery in not possible. 
>> Manual snapshot is stored in S3. 
>> Manual snapshot is not deleted automatically , when DB instance is deleted. Need to delete manually . 
>> Take final snapshot before deleting RDS DB, for future reference. 
>> Manual snapshot can be share directly with other AWS account users. 
>> When DB is recovered from snapshot , then recovered DB has default intial settings . for eg old phone data transfer to new phone. 
>> Manual DB snaphot can't be restored on existing running DB, it should be run on new DB instance. 
>> Restoring from DB snapshot changes RDS instance endpoint ( url or IP address )  .
>> At the time of restoring , you can change the storage  type .

** DB encryption 
>> You can't encrypt existing unencrypted DB instance. 
>> To do that 
   create new instance and while creating make it encrypted and migrate data to it. 
   or 
   You can take snapshot , and recovery from snapshot and keep it encrypted while recovery . 
>> RDS supports encryption at rest for all DB engines using KMS. 

** What actually encrypted when at rest 
>> all it's snapshot. 
>> Backup of DB . 
>> Data on EBS volume. 
>> Read replica created from the snapshot. 


